; ============================================================
; Sample Configuration File for simple-backup.bat
; ============================================================
;
; HOW TO USE:
;   1. Uncomment a line by removing the leading semicolon (;).
;   2. Replace the example value after the '=' with your own.
;   3. Save this file in the same folder as simple-backup.bat.
;
; NOTE: All lines in this sample are commented out by default.
;       The script will prompt you for any missing values at runtime.
;
; SPACES IN VALUES:
;   You do NOT need to wrap values in quotes. Spaces are fine.
;   Example: SOURCE=C:\Users\John Doe\Documents
; ============================================================

; --------------------------------------------------------------
; SOURCE
;   The folder on your local computer that you want to back up.
;   You can use an absolute path or a relative path.
; --------------------------------------------------------------
;SOURCE=C:\Users\John\Documents\Important
;SOURCE=C:\Users\John Doe\Documents

; --------------------------------------------------------------
; DESTINATION
;   The network path (UNC) where backups will be stored.
;   Example: \\NAS\Backups\MyFolder or \\192.168.1.50\backup
; --------------------------------------------------------------
;DESTINATION=\\192.168.1.50\backup\john_docs

; --------------------------------------------------------------
; USERNAME
;   The username for authenticating to the network share.
;   If omitted, the script will prompt you to enter it.
; --------------------------------------------------------------
;USERNAME=nas_user

; --------------------------------------------------------------
; LOG_DIR
;   The folder where backup log files will be saved.
;   If omitted, logs are written to the script's current directory.
; --------------------------------------------------------------
;LOG_DIR=C:\Users\John\BackupLogs
